    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d93">

                <pb facs="0196" n="126" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg126"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 290.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-07-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 8, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> As inquiry may be made of you as to the
                    approbation by this government of a treaty recently concluded by Mr. Corwin with
                    the government of Mexico, by one of the stipulations of which a sum of money was
                    to be paid to that government, I have to inform you that the instrument was
                    submitted to the Senate, but the Committee on Foreign Relations of that body has
                    reported adversely thereon. It is not probable, therefore, that at this session
                    at least the Senate will advise and consent to the ratification of the
                    treaty.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                    <p rendition="#center">[Same to W. L. Dayton, No. 177.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
